From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:05:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScript: document.all, image state, interface names,
 observer fixes

document.all is a collection with [[IsHTMLDDA]] (QuickJS's
JS_SetIsHTMLDDA through markHTMLDDA): it was undefined, so x ===
document.all held for every undefined x (YouTube's sanitizer replaced
undefined bound values with "zClosurez" and hid its results).
<img> complete, naturalWidth, naturalHeight (imageState).  Interface
objects have names (constructor.name was "").
IntersectionObserverEntry members are prototype getters (a polyfill
replaced the observer otherwise); an element that intersects without
area gets another entry once it has area.  The timers this file uses
are the bindings' own, not what a page put on window.  Computed styles
skip inline keywords and var() values.
